{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":1.0,"text":"About one in four older adults may be low on water and not even feel thirsty. Grandma seems foggy or dizzy? We blame old age, but it could just be dehydration. With age, the brain's thirst signal gets slower and weaker, and the body stores less water. In one study, after a day without water, older men were more dehydrated than young men, yet less thirsty. So offer sips all day. Don't wait for thirst. Heart or kidney condition? Ask your doctor first. Who in your family forgets to drink? Tell me in the comments.","words":[{"text":"About","start":0.0,"end":0.3,"type":"word","logprob":-3.4570634852570947e-6,"characters":[{"text":"A","start":0.0,"end":0.08},{"text":"b","start":0.08,"end":0.16},{"text":"o","start":0.16,"end":0.16},{"text":"u","start":0.16,"end":0.26},{"text":"t","start":0.26,"end":0.3}]},{"text":" ","start":0.3,"end":0.36,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.00023398046323563904,"characters":[{"text":" ","start":0.3,"end":0.36}]},{"text":"one","start":0.36,"end":0.48,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00023398046323563904,"characters":[{"text":"o","start":0.36,"end":0.4},{"text":"n","start":0.42,"end":0.42},{"text":"e","start":0.44,"end":0.48}]},{"text":" ","start":0.48,"end":0.52,"type":"spacing","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7,"characters":[{"text":" ","start":0.48,"end":0.52}]},{"text":"in","start":0.52,"end":0.7,"type":"word","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7,"characters":[{"text":"i","start":0.52,"end":0.6},{"text":"n","start":0.6,"end":0.7}]},{"text":" ","start":0.7,"end":0.76,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7,"characters":[{"text":" ","start":0.7,"end":0.76}]},{"text":"four","start":0.76,"end":0.94,"type":"word","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7,"characters":[{"text":"f","start":0.76,"end":0.8},{"text":"o","start":0.8,"end":0.82},{"text":"u","start":0.82,"end":0.86},{"text":"r","start":0.92,"end":0.94}]},{"text":" ","start":0.94,"end":1.08,"type":"spacing","logprob":-3.576278118089249e-7,"ch